[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441938126","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4035#issuecomment-441938126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4035","id":441938126,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTkzODEyNg==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-28T19:08:04Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:11:21Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nSo #3937 is where we got hit with this, because on my end I could find no other way of detecting if cx_Oracle was built with the ancient \"WITH_UNICODE\" flag unless I noticed that cx_Oracle.UNICODE was missing.   Fast forward a few years to 5.3 where you removed cx_Oracle.UNICODE entirely, and everyone's SQLAlchemy broke.    So apparently I read that as, \"unicode mode is switched on unconditionally\", when really it meant, \"there is no more unicode mode\" :).   which is better !   \n\nThe flag for WITH_UNICODE is now blocked if cx_Oracle version >= (5, 3) in https://gerrit.sqlalchemy.org/461.\n\nin particular if you can confirm this comment:\n\n            # cx_Oracle WITH_UNICODE mode.  *only* python\n            # unicode objects accepted for anything.  This\n            # mode of operation is implicit for Python 3,\n            # however under Python 2 it existed as a never-used build-time\n            # option for cx_Oracle 5.0 - 5.2 and was removed as of 5.3.\n\nBasically when 5.3 is present, we go in full \"python 2\" operation like WITH_UNICODE never existed.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441938126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441938133","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/